@@ -3,3 +3,17 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "json-toolkit";
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+resolvePointer(doc, ""); // the whole document
+```
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value a pointer refers to. It throws a `SyntaxError` if
+`pointer` is not a valid JSON Pointer (RFC 6901 §3), and an `Error` if it does not resolve to a value of
+the document: missing member, array index out of range, leading zeros, or `-` (§4). `null` is a value and
+resolves normally. Only own properties are followed, and the document is never modified.
