+---
+id: task-001-json-pointer-resolvepointer-rfc-6901
+type: task
+title: "JSON Pointer resolvePointer (RFC 6901)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Task
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) and export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+
+- Returns the value the pointer refers to (RFC 6901 §4 evaluation).
+- Throws if the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer (§3 syntax: empty string, or `/`-prefixed tokens; `~` only as `~0`/`~1`).
+- Throws if the pointer does not resolve to a value (missing member, out-of-range or invalid array index, non-container). `null` values resolve normally.
+- Escapes decoded `~1` -> `/` first, then `~0` -> `~` (§4).
+- Array indexes: `0` or digits without leading zero; `-` refers to a nonexistent element, so it throws (§4).
+- Only own properties are followed (no prototype pollution/leak via `__proto__`, `constructor`).
+- Input is never mutated. Tests under `test/` cover the RFC's §5 examples and edge cases; README updated.
